# Phase 278 Compact Criterion Review

**Status**: Supporting reference
**Supersedes**: N/A
**Referenced by**: [Mac validation](../README.md), [Phase 278](../../../phase-278-external-bars-no-self-referential-gate-lint-and-exact-served.md)
**Generated sections**: none

> **Purpose**: Preserve the prospective independent justification and concrete
> implementation boundaries for the user's selected compact supervised recipes.

The user selects the documented compact graphs and unchanged per-run budgets.
The [reviewed revision-2 contract](raw/proposal/revision-2/contract.md.txt) defines
five actual training seeds, canonical base plus **0..4**, with index **0** fixed
as the served model. At least three runs must jointly improve over their own
initial predictor and pass the defined trivial-reference control. The median
uses all five final metrics and the exact unchanged historical floors; the
served model independently passes every per-artifact requirement. Finite
below-floor outcomes remain evidence and never become eligible checkpoints.

The [independent scope review](raw/independent-review/scope-review.md.txt) checks
the exact rule and its limits. Classification uses alpha **1/5000**, giving
critical counts **136 / 24 / 16** for **10 / 100 / 200** semantic classes and
1,000 examples, before the stricter majority condition. The stated **0.01**
bound covers at most thirty all-five-null cohorts with independent uniform
guesses within each seed's evaluation; it needs no cross-seed independence. It
does not establish population generalization, signal in arbitrary random
networks, or published-model parity. Regression and paired improvement are
descriptive exact comparisons on the pinned examples.

Historical accuracy/RMSE floors remain additional restrictions with their true
provenance. Tiny's `0.008` is measurement-calibrated; the new rule does not
retroactively make it an external published anchor. Exit Definitions 6/26 and
the engineering contract now state this prospective scope explicitly. The SL
decision does not independently justify unrelated RL slack.

The [implementation design](raw/proposal/revision-2/implementation-design.md.txt)
requires typed singleton child plans, actual initial snapshots, all-five raw
outcomes, replay and authenticated journal binding. Its original detached-proof
design remains retained. The later [sidecar binding review](raw/independent-review/detached-sidecar-binding.md.txt)
clarifies that checkpoint-scope digest binds the root path, not file contents:
the sidecar needs explicit producer/report/journal authentication. Supervised
Store admission keeps its prohibition on companion pointers.

The [manifest](manifest.json) inventories both historical proposal versions,
exact arithmetic and independent notes. Its verification receipt, stdout/stderr
and duplicated prior-original members are local-only diagnostics excluded from
Git and Docker contexts; this historical
inventory is not a complete clean-checkout bundle. The reviewed contract,
arithmetic, rationale and selected criterion data remain versioned. These are
prospective reviews. Implementation,
actual five-run qualification and Phase 278 closure
remain incomplete; no past singleton journal is relabelled as new evidence.

The later [private implementation preparation](../runtime-receipts/compact-stage123-preparation/README.md)
passes its scoped policy/plan/snapshot controls. It preserves this proposal's
historical scope and supplies no complete publisher, authenticated lane or actual
five-run qualification evidence.
